The list of originals holds every value the pseudonymizer replaced, and not
all of them identify anyone.
A student's city ([[Postort]]) is replaced as contact data, and the words of
a free-text note are replaced with it.
The first recording found such values hundreds of times: a city in the
names of courses given there, a short word in the translation table, and
[[POST]] as the method of the write requests.

Finding a value in LADOK's own public text says nothing about a person, so
when we scan a cassette we allow the originals that occur in the public text
of \emph{that cassette}: in course and code-table names ([[Benamning]] and
its [[sv]] and [[en]] texts), in codes ([[Kod]]), in the translation table
([[Text]]), and as HTTP methods.
Responses from the code tables, the translation table and the course
information ([[PUBLIC_PATHS]]) hold no people, so all of their text counts as
public.
So do the HTTP headers, apart from cookies and credentials: a short word
recorded as an original once turned up in every cassette, as the [[max]] of
[[Cache-Control: max-age=0]].
The staff lists, which the catalogue service also serves, are not among them.
Allowing per cassette matters: the table of Swedish places holds many words
that are also surnames, and allowing those in every cassette would let a
surname that the scrubber missed in a student's record go unnoticed.
Within one cassette, a surname that is also a word in a course name there is
still allowed; that is the price of not reading the cassettes by eye.

The cassettes store characters outside ASCII escaped, as in
[[Malm\xF6]], and the scan reads the file as it is stored, so it sees the
part before an escape as a word of its own; we therefore also take the words
of the public text in its escaped form, with the escapes themselves taken
out, or the [[n]] of an escaped line break would stick to the next word.
<<scan the recordings for personal data>>=
originals = vcr_support.read_list(getattr(config, "_originals_path", None))
written_files = [path for _, written in sorted(pairs)
                 for path in vcr_support.iter_files([written])
                 if path.name != LIVE_MARKER_FILE]
needles = vcr_support.Needles(originals)
leaks = []
for path in written_files:
  allow = public_originals(originals, path)
  leaks += [(path, where, kind, hit)
            for where, kind, hit in vcr_support.scan_file(path, needles,
                                                          allow=allow)]
if leaks:
  write("PRIVACY: the recordings contain personal data or secrets (values "
        "redacted below). Extend the key lists in testing.nw, delete the "
        "cassettes, and record again.", red=True)
  for path, where, kind, hit in leaks:
    write(f"  {path}:{where}: {kind} {hit}")
  session.exitstatus = 1
